Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>

This covers the two annotation layers this repository adds — the drift schedule
(`results/drift_events.json`, `src/t13/drift.py`, `src/t13/drift_params.json`) and the
endogenous label-arrival model (`src/t13/arrival.py`) — together with every derived
artefact under `results/`.

### Attribution for the source dataset

These layers are derived from, and are a derivative work of:

> Sharma, Abhishek. *SynB2B-Fraud: A Synthetic Dataset for Fraud Detection in B2B
> Payment Networks.* Zenodo, 29 July 2026. DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.21668281.
> Licensed CC BY 4.0.

The source dataset is not redistributed here. `make reproduce-full` fetches it from
Zenodo at run time. SynB2B-Fraud is fully synthetic; no real payment records, no
real buyer or supplier identities and no third-party data are contained in it.

Anyone redistributing this repository's derived data must keep the attribution above,
note that changes were made, and pass on the CC BY 4.0 terms.

